    "id": "builder_blog:builder_blog:https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/25/ruff/#atom-everything",
    "source": "builder_blog",
    "sourceItemId": "builder_blog:https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/25/ruff/#atom-everything",
    "title": "Ruff v0.16.0",
    "summary": "<p><strong><a href=\"https://astral.sh/blog/ruff-v0.16.0\">Ruff v0.16.0</a></strong></p> Astral shipped a significant new version of their Ruff Python linting tool a few days ago on July 23rd. I noticed today because my various CI jobs all started failing thanks to new default Ruff checks and my unpinned <code>\"ruff\"</code> dev dependency.</p> <p>From Brent Westbrook's announcement post:</p> <blockquote> <p>Ruff now enables 413 rules by default, up from 59 in previous versions.</p> <p>Since Ruff's",
    "body": "<p><strong><a href=\"https://astral.sh/blog/ruff-v0.16.0\">Ruff v0.16.0</a></strong></p> Astral shipped a significant new version of their Ruff Python linting tool a few days ago on July 23rd. I noticed today because my various CI jobs all started failing thanks to new default Ruff checks and my unpinned <code>\"ruff\"</code> dev dependency.</p> <p>From Brent Westbrook's announcement post:</p> <blockquote> <p>Ruff now enables 413 rules by default, up from 59 in previous versions.</p> <p>Since Ruff's default rule set was last modified in <a href=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/main/changelogs/0.1.x.md#breaking-changes\">v0.1.0</a>, the number of rules in Ruff has grown from 708 to 968. Many of these rules catch severe issues, including <a href=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/load-befo",
    "url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/25/ruff/#atom-everything",
    "sourceName": "Simon Willison",
